Feature: Mask the last 4 digits of invoice numbers in the d_product_revenue_clone table

  Background:
    Given the d_product_revenue table exists
    And the d_product_revenue_clone table may or may not exist

  Scenario: Setup clone table
    Given the d_product_revenue_clone table exists
    When the table is dropped
    Then a new d_product_revenue_clone table should replicate the d_product_revenue table structure

  Scenario Outline: Mask last 4 digits of invoice_number
    Given the d_product_revenue_clone table has invoice_number column with format <Invoice_Format>
    When I mask the last 4 digits of invoice numbers
    Then the invoice_number should be updated to <Masked_Invoice_Number>

  Examples:
    | Invoice_Format | Masked_Invoice_Number |
    | 1234234534     | 123423****            |
    | A234R98234     | A234R9****            |
    | 9876543210     | 987654****            |

  Scenario: Handle non-standard invoice_number formats
    Given a non-standard invoice_number format in the d_product_revenue_clone table
    When an attempt is made to mask the last 4 digits
    Then an error "Invalid format for invoice_number" should be logged

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario for missing permissions
    Given access is restricted for modifying the d_product_revenue_clone table
    When I attempt to update the invoice_number column
    Then the error "Insufficient permissions to modify table" should be raised

  Examples:
    | Description            |
    | Insufficient Data Owner permissions |
    | Read-only access mode  |

  Scenario: Check compatibility with PySpark version
    Given the PySpark version in use is <Version>
    When code execution starts
    Then it should be compatible without version-specific errors

  Examples:
    | Version  |
    | 3.0.1    |
    | 3.1.2    |
    | 3.2.0    |
